## part 4
```java
public class TemperaturePractice {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double celsius = 35;
        double fahrenheit = (9.0 / 5.0) * celsius + 32;

        System.out.println("Celsius: " + celsius);
        System.out.println("Fahrenheit: " + fahrenheit);
    }
}
```

The (9 / 5) had 67.0 F
The (9.0 / 5.0) had 95.0 F
This happened because with integers java removes the decimal point so 1.8 became 1
floating-point keeps the decimal point and thats why there is sucha drastic diffrence.

